       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum recommended daily dose is 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg for extended-release. This order is double that limit. It raises the risk of serious GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nCan you tell me which of these you meant?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **Another dose.** If you meant something else, for example 1700 mg total per day, tell me and I'll adjust it.\n\nIf the 1700 mg three times daily dose is intentional, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
